---
title: Sour Cream Sugar Cookies
author: Aunt Lena Thorson
category: Cookies
cook time: 10 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@shortening{0.5%cup}
@sugar{1.25%cups}
@sour cream{1%cup}
@baking powder{1%tsp}
@salt{0.5%tsp}
@vanilla{1%tsp}
@soften butter{0.5%cup}
@eggs{2}
@flour{4%cups}
@baking soda{1%tsp}
@nutmeg{1%tsp}

Cream shortening, butter and sugar. Add salt, vanilla, nutmeg and unbeaten eggs. Blend well. Add sour cream alternately with remaining dry ingredients. Chill 1 hour or overnight. Roll thin and cut with cookie cutter. Sprinkle with sugar. Bake at 400 degrees for 10 minutes. Makes 3 dozen large or 6 dozen small cookies.
